.TH BOSWAS-COMPOSITOR 1 "November 2026" "Boswas OS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
boswas-compositor \- the Boswas OS Wayland compositor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B boswas-compositor
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fB\-\-\fR \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B boswas-compositor
is the display server, window manager and effects engine of the Boswas OS
desktop. It draws every window, routes all input, and decides which program
may see or control what. Applications connect to it with the standard
Wayland protocols.
.PP
It is normally started by
.BR boswas-session (1).
Once it accepts clients it starts the shell
.RB ( boswas-shell (1))
as a trusted client and restarts it if it exits.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-backend " KIND"
\fBudev\fR: real hardware (DRM/KMS, libinput, libseat); the default on a
virtual terminal.
\fBwinit\fR: a window inside another Wayland or X11 session; the default
there.
\fBheadless\fR: one output rendered in software into memory, for tests.
.TP
.BI \-\-headless\-size " WIDTH" x HEIGHT
Size of the headless output (default 1920x1080).
.TP
.BI \-\-socket " NAME"
Wayland socket name (default: the first free \fBwayland\-\fIN\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-config " FILE"
Read only this configuration file instead of the three layers below.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-shell
Do not start the shell.
.TP
.B \-\-test\-input
Accept input-injection commands on trusted control connections. For tests.
.TP
.B \-\-print\-env
Print \fBWAYLAND_DISPLAY\fR and \fBBOSWAS_COMPOSITOR_SOCKET\fR on standard
output once the compositor is ready.
.TP
.BI \-\-send " COMMAND"
Send a command to a running compositor's control socket, print the reply
and exit: \fBversion\fR, \fBlock\fR or \fBreload\-config\fR. With
\fB\-\-control\-socket\fR \fIPATH\fR another compositor's socket is used.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a summary of the options.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH KEYBOARD AND POINTER
.TS
tab(|);
l l.
Super|open or close the launcher
Super+L|lock the session
Alt+Tab, Alt+Shift+Tab|switch windows, most recently used first
Alt+F4|close the window
Super+Up|maximize
Super+Down|restore; minimize a floating window
Super+Left, Super+Right|snap to the left or right half
Super+F11|fullscreen
Super+1 ... Super+4|switch workspace
Super+Shift+1 ... 4|move the window to a workspace
Super+E|file manager
Ctrl+Alt+T|terminal
Ctrl+Alt+F1 ... F12|switch virtual terminal
.TE
.PP
Drag a title bar to move a window; drag it to a screen edge for a snap
layout (top: maximize; sides: halves; the outer quarter of a side: that
corner). Double-click a title bar to maximize. Drag the border to resize.
Super+left drag moves and Super+right drag resizes from anywhere on a
window. Shortcuts use the key's position on the Latin layout, so they work
the same while another layout is active.
.SH CONFIGURATION
TOML files, later ones overriding earlier ones key by key:
.PP
.nf
/usr/share/boswas/compositor/compositor.toml   shipped defaults
/etc/boswas/compositor.toml                    the administrator
~/.config/boswas/compositor.toml               the user
~/.config/boswas/appearance.toml               written by boswas\-preset
.fi
.PP
A file that does not parse, or that contains an unknown key, is reported and
ignored as a whole. \fIappearance.toml\fR may contain the [appearance] table
only.
.TP
.B [keyboard]
\fBlayout\fR, \fBvariant\fR, \fBmodel\fR, \fBoptions\fR (XKB names, for
example layout "us,in" with options "grp:alt_shift_toggle");
\fBrepeat_delay\fR (milliseconds), \fBrepeat_rate\fR (per second).
.TP
.B [pointer]
\fBnatural_scroll\fR, \fBtap_to_click\fR, \fBaccel_speed\fR (\-1.0 to 1.0),
\fBcursor_theme\fR, \fBcursor_size\fR.
.TP
.B [output]
\fBscale\fR: 1.0, 1.25, 1.5, 1.75 or 2.0, for every output.
.TP
.B [lock]
\fBidle_seconds\fR: time without input before the session locks (0: never,
if the policy allows it). \fBcommand\fR: the lock screen program (read
from the first two files only).
.TP
.B [shell]
\fBcommand\fR: the shell program (read from the first two files only).
These two programs are started as trusted clients, so a user's file cannot
name them.
.TP
.B [apps]
\fBterminal\fR and \fBfiles\fR: the programs of Ctrl+Alt+T and Super+E.
.TP
.B [appearance]
\fBscheme\fR ("dark" or "light"), \fBreduced_motion\fR, \fBwallpaper\fR (a
PNG or JPEG file shown by the shell instead of the default background).
.TP
.B [policy]
Read from the first two files only; ignored in a user's file.
\fBlock_idle_max_seconds\fR: the longest lock timeout a user may choose (0:
no limit). \fBprivileged_protocols\fR: "shell" (default) or "all" (see
SECURITY).
.SH SECURITY
Ordinary clients get the application protocols only: they cannot read the
screen, other windows or global key strokes.
.PP
The privileged protocols (layer shell for panels and overlays, session
lock, the window list, clipboard control) are offered only to programs the
compositor started itself, over a connection it created for them. Clients
that connect through a security context (Flatpak and other sandboxes) never
get them. \fBprivileged_protocols = "all"\fR offers them to every client
outside a sandbox; it exists for development and must not be set on a
managed device.
.PP
The compositor owns the session lock. Locking blanks every output and takes
input away from applications before the lock screen is started; only a lock
client's unlock request ends it. If the lock screen exits without
unlocking, the outputs stay blank and it is started again. The session is
also locked before the system suspends or hibernates
(\fI/usr/lib/systemd/system\-sleep/boswas\-lock\fR).
.PP
The compositor runs as the logged-in user. Device access comes from the
login session (libseat, logind); it has no setuid bit and needs no
capability.
.SH CONTROL SOCKET
\fB$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/boswas\-\fIWAYLAND_DISPLAY\fB.sock\fR accepts one JSON
object per line. Connections to this socket may ask for \fBversion\fR,
\fBlock\fR and \fBreload\-config\fR. The window list, window control, workspaces, screenshots and
\fBquit\fR are available to the shell only, on the descriptor the
compositor hands it.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BOSWAS_LOG
Log filter (for example \fBdebug\fR or \fBboswas_compositor=trace\fR).
Messages go to standard error.
.TP
.B XCURSOR_THEME
Cursor theme when \fBpointer.cursor_theme\fR is empty.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when the session ended normally, 1 when the compositor could not start or
failed, 2 for a usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR boswas-session (1),
.BR boswas-shell (1),
.BR greetd (1)
